{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"earthen-flayed-baboon","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nFollow-up (fix b) discovered during creatable-foldable-arthropods (fix a, merged as a0fc8d43556 / Gerrit 1761). Fix (a) stopped the runaway-loop guard from counting memo-served repeats as loop evidence. A second, independent defect remains in the completion verifier's evidence-banking path: at SEARCH EXHAUSTION, `BOUNDED_FALLBACK_EVIDENCE` banks `met=false` — i.e. \"the criterion is unmet\" — when what the run actually established is only \"the search budget ran out before sufficient evidence was found\". Banking a hard negative from an exhausted search misattributes absence-of-evidence as evidence-of-absence: subsequent verifier passes (and the close gate) treat the criterion as affirmatively failed, producing false FAIL verdicts on tickets whose evidence exists but was not reached within the window.\n\n## Proposed fix\nMake the banked evidence TRI-STATE: `met=true`, `met=false` (a positive refutation was actually found), and `insufficient_evidence` (search exhausted / budget hit / window truncated without a determination). At search exhaustion, `BOUNDED_FALLBACK_EVIDENCE` must bank `insufficient_evidence`, never `met=false`. Downstream consumers (verdict composer, close gate messaging) must distinguish the two: `insufficient_evidence` yields an INDETERMINATE-style outcome with the existing remediation messaging (re-verify, widen scope, or operator-attest), not a FAIL.\n\n## Scope\n- The evidence-banking site(s) in the completion-verifier workflow where BOUNDED_FALLBACK_EVIDENCE is constructed at exhaustion.\n- The evidence schema/consumer seam that renders per-criterion verdicts from banked evidence.\n- Tests: a search-exhaustion run banks insufficient_evidence (not met=false); a genuine refutation still banks met=false; verdict rendering distinguishes the two.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [ ] At search exhaustion, banked fallback evidence is `insufficient_evidence`, not `met=false`; checked by a new unit test.\n- [ ] A genuine positive refutation still banks `met=false` and still yields FAIL; checked by a guard test.\n- [ ] Verdict composition renders `insufficient_evidence` as indeterminate-with-remediation, not FAIL; checked by a rendering test.\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` clean; lands via Gerrit (LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1) before close.\n\n## Out of scope\nGuard/memo interaction (fix a, landed); verifier prompt changes; retry policy.","id":"1d71-a76c-04f6-4642","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Completion verifier banks met=false at search exhaustion — should bank insufficient_evidence (tri-state)"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786694355830665001,"uuid":"3d95b7a5-43e0-4e48-8463-a4f52f381c36"}